cff-version: 1.2.0
title: orpheus
abstract: >-
  A python package for the calculation of second-, third- and fourth-order
  correlation functions of scalar and polar fields such as weak lensing shear.
  The N>2 correlators are computed through a multipole decomposition, with the
  heavy lifting carried out by parallelised C kernels.
message: >-
  As there is currently no dedicated orpheus paper, please cite the paper that
  introduced the functionality you use. The list is given in the README and in
  the documentation at https://orpheus.readthedocs.io/.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Porth
    given-names: Lucas
version: 0.5.2
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/lporth93/orpheus"
url: "https://orpheus.readthedocs.io/"
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - weak gravitational lensing
  - correlation functions
  - aperture mass
  - intrinsic alignments